name: Cancel historical Git inspection without writing baselines
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 PATH=@ART/git-bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME prepare
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 15 LOGS | settled-logs
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME arm
submit: run coverage:sweep {"writeSkips":true}
require-live-snap: 15 Ctrl+C request abort | active-inspection
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME blocked
live-snap: blocked-git
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME request
keys: C-c
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME canceled
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 15 cancelled || canceled || Cancelled || Canceled | canceled-inspection
ask: Does cancellation stop the owned Git adapter, preserve baseline history and leave the shell available for an explicit retry?
submit: run coverage:sweep {"writeSkips":true}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 1 skip row(s) written | explicit-retry
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME completed
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: reader-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: reader-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: reader-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: reader-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: reader-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: reader-tail-40x12
ask: Are cancellation, explicit retry and historical source meaning readable across the six sizes without claiming a scan or finding fix?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: run coverage:baselines {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Historical Git baseline records | recovered-records
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/coverage_cancellation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME completed
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the successful explicit retry and the original history, without provider work or source execution?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
